3 Samuel then said to all the house of Israel, “If you return to the Lord with all your heart, leave aside the foreign gods and the Astartes that are among you;
direct your hearts towards the Lord and serve him alone. Thus the Lord
He will deliver from the power of the Philistines.

19 For your heart has been moved and you have humbled yourself before the Lord when you heard what I said against this place and against its inhabitants, namely, that they will become a devastation and a curse;
Because you have torn your clothes and wept before me, I too have
heard –oracle of the Lord–.

8 Hanamel, my uncle's son, came to me in the court of the guard, according to the word of the Lord, and said to me, "Buy me my field which is in Anathoth, in the country of Benjamin, for you have the right
of acquisition and rescue: buy it from me. I understood that that was the word
of the Lord;

17 As for you, son of man, this is what the Lord says: Say to all the birds and all the wild beasts: Gather together and come! Gather from everywhere for the sacrifice that I offer you, a great
sacrifice on the mountains of Israel. You will eat meat and drink
blood;

13 Therefore, my son, prefer your brothers; do not be proud of the sons and daughters of your people, refusing to take a wife among them. Because pride brings
ruin and great disorder, and idleness leads to decay and misery;
she is, in effect, the mother of penury.

11 He abolished the humanitarian privileges that the kings had granted to the Jews, through John, father of Eupolemus, the same Eupolemus who was sent as an ambassador to make a
alliance of friendship with the Romans; abrogated legal institutions and
introduced new customs contrary to the Law;
